              >
                2.1
              </div>
              <h3 className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                Discovery of Subatomic Particles
              </h3>
            </div>

            <div className={proseClass}>
              <p className="lead text-xl text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium mb-8">
                For centuries the atom was thought to be indivisible. Then
                experiments with electric currents and gas-discharge tubes
                revealed that the atom itself has an internal structure.
              </p>

              <p>
                Three subatomic particles build every atom: the negatively
                charged <strong>electron</strong>, the positively charged{" "}
                <strong>proton</strong>, and the neutral{" "}
                <strong>neutron</strong>. Their discovery happened over more
                than three decades, each experiment sharpening the picture of
                what matter is made of.
              </p>

              {/* Particle Cards */}
              <div className="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 my-8">
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-green-100 dark:border-green-800/60 bg-green-50/50 dark:bg-green-900/10 p-5">
