              {/* Key Concept: Anatomy of the Atom */}
              <div className="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 my-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-xl">
                  <Target className="text-green-500" />
                  Key Concept: Anatomy of the Atom
                </h4>
                <div className="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[230px_1fr] md:items-center">
                  <div className="relative mx-auto flex h-52 w-52 items-center justify-center">
                    <div className="absolute inset-0 rounded-full border-2 border-dashed border-green-300 dark:border-green-700/60" />
                    <div className="absolute inset-8 rounded-full border-2 border-dashed border-teal-300 dark:border-teal-700/60" />
                    <div className="absolute inset-16 rounded-full border-2 border-dashed border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-700/60" />
                    <div className="relative flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-green-500 to-teal-600 text-[10px] font-bold text-white shadow-lg">
                      p⁺ n⁰
                    </div>
                    {[
                      "top-[16%] left-[30%]",
                      "top-[8%] left-[58%]",
                      "top-[40%] left-[10%]",
                      "bottom-[18%] left-[22%]",
                      "bottom-[10%] right-[30%]",
                      "top-[30%] right-[10%]",
                      "bottom-[34%] right-[14%]",
                    ].map((position) => (
                      <span
                        key={position}
                        className={`absolute h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 shadow-sm ${position}`}
                      />
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-3 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li className="flex gap-3">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-green-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong className="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                          Nucleus:
                        </strong>{" "}
                        protons and neutrons packed into about 10⁻¹⁵ m. It
                        holds more than 99.9% of the atom's mass.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li className="flex gap-3">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong className="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                          Electron cloud:
                        </strong>{" "}
                        electrons occupy quantized orbitals around the nucleus.
                        The whole atom is about 10⁻¹⁰ m across.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li className="flex gap-3">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-emerald-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong className="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                          Neutral atom:
                        </strong>{" "}
                        number of protons equals number of electrons. Ions form
                        when electrons are gained or lost.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              {/* Real World Example */}
              <div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 to-orange-50 dark:from-amber-900/20 dark:to-orange-900/20 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 my-8 border border-amber-200/50 dark:border-amber-700/30">
                <div className="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div className="p-3 bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-800/50 rounded-xl text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mt-1">
                    <Lightbulb size={24} />
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 className="text-lg font-bold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300 mb-2 m-0">
                      Real-World Example: Cathode Rays in Your Living Room
                    </h4>
                    <p className="m-0 text-amber-800/80 dark:text-amber-200/80 leading-relaxed">
                      Old CRT televisions and computer monitors worked by firing
                      a beam of electrons at a phosphor-coated screen. The same
                      cathode-ray physics that revealed the electron in 1897
                      powered displays for almost a century — and helped launch
                      the entire electronics industry.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <Exercise
                number="2.1"
                accent="green"
                question={
                  <p className="m-0">
                    An atom contains 16 protons, 16 electrons, and 18 neutrons.
                    Identify the element, its atomic number (Z), its mass number
                    (A), and its overall charge.
                  </p>
                }
                answer={
                  <div className="space-y-2">
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>Element:</strong> sulfur (S), because Z = 16.
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>Atomic number:</strong> Z = 16.
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>Mass number:</strong> A = protons + neutrons = 16
                      + 18 = 34 (sulfur-34).
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>Charge:</strong> 16 protons and 16 electrons
                      cancel, so the atom is neutral (charge 0).
                    </p>
                  </div>
                }
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Section 2.2 */}
        <motion.section
          variants={itemVariants}
          id="subtopic-2.2"
          className="scroll-mt-24"
        >
          <div className={cardClass}>
            <div className={sectionHeaderClass}>
              <div
                className={`${numberBoxClass} bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400`}
              >
                2.2
              </div>
              <h3 className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                Atomic Models
              </h3>
            </div>

            <div className={proseClass}>
              <p className="lead text-xl text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium mb-8">
                Every atomic model is a useful story that explains some
                evidence — until a new experiment reveals what the story cannot
                explain.
              </p>

              <p>
                Atomic theory did not appear fully formed. It evolved as
                physicists fired particles at matter and watched how they
                scattered. Each model below kept what worked and replaced what
                failed.
              </p>

              <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">
                <Clock className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-500" />
                A timeline of atomic models
              </h4>

              <div className="space-y-4 my-6">
                {atomicModels.map((model, index) => (
                  <div
                    key={model.year}
                    className="grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_1fr] gap-4"
                  >
                    <div className="flex flex-col items-center">
                      <div className="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-sm font-bold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
                        {index + 1}
                      </div>
                      {index < atomicModels.length - 1 && (
                        <div className="mt-2 w-0.5 flex-1 bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-200 to-transparent dark:from-blue-800" />
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <div className="mb-2 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/40 p-5">
                      <div className="mb-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
                        <span className="rounded-full bg-blue-600 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-bold tracking-wide text-white">
                          {model.year}
                        </span>
                        <h4 className="m-0 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                          {model.title}
                        </h4>
                      </div>
                      <p className="m-0 mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                        {model.idea}
                      </p>
                      <p className="m-0 text-xs text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400">
                        <span className="font-bold">Limitation:</span>{" "}
                        {model.limitation}
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              {/* Rutherford Experiment */}
              <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-10 mb-4">
                <Radiation className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-500" />
                Rutherford's gold-foil experiment (1909–1911)
              </h4>

              <p>
                Rutherford's team (Geiger and Marsden) fired positively charged
                alpha particles at an extremely thin gold foil and recorded
                where they landed on a zinc-sulfide screen.
              </p>

              <div className="my-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-5">
                <div className="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between">
                  <div className="text-center">
                    <div className="mx-auto mb-2 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/40 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">
                      <Radiation size={22} />
                    </div>
                    <p className="m-0 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      Alpha source
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <ArrowRight className="h-5 w-5 rotate-90 text-rose-400 sm:rotate-0" />
                  <div className="text-center">
                    <div className="mx-auto mb-2 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-yellow-100 dark:bg-yellow-900/40 text-sm font-bold text-yellow-700 dark:text-yellow-300">
                      Au
                    </div>
                    <p className="m-0 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      Gold foil
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <ArrowRight className="h-5 w-5 rotate-90 text-rose-400 sm:rotate-0" />
                  <div className="text-center">
                    <div className="mx-auto mb-2 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">
                      ZnS
                    </div>
                    <p className="m-0 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      Detector screen
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div className="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 my-6">
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-green-100 dark:border-green-800/60 bg-green-50/50 dark:bg-green-900/10 p-4">
                  <p className="m-0 mb-1 text-2xl font-black text-green-600 dark:text-green-400">
                    Most
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                    passed straight through
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                    The atom is mostly empty space.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100 dark:border-amber-800/60 bg-amber-50/50 dark:bg-amber-900/10 p-4">
                  <p className="m-0 mb-1 text-2xl font-black text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">
                    Some
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                    deflected at small angles
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                    Positive charge is concentrated somewhere.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-rose-100 dark:border-rose-800/60 bg-rose-50/50 dark:bg-rose-900/10 p-4">
                  <p className="m-0 mb-1 text-2xl font-black text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400">
                    ≈ 1 in 20,000
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                    bounced back
                  </p>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                    A tiny, massive, positive nucleus deflected them.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div className="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/60 bg-emerald-50/60 dark:bg-emerald-900/15 p-5 my-6">
                <h4 className="m-0 mb-2 text-base font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300">
                  Conclusion: the nuclear model
                </h4>
                <p className="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                  Nearly all the atom's mass and all of its positive charge sit
                  in a minute nucleus. The nucleus is roughly 10⁻¹⁵ m across
                  while the atom is about 10⁻¹⁰ m — if the atom were a football
                  stadium, the nucleus would be a marble at the centre.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div className="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 dark:border-rose-800/60 bg-rose-50/60 dark:bg-rose-900/15 p-5 my-6">
                <h4 className="m-0 mb-2 text-base font-bold text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-300">
                  Why the nuclear model was incomplete
                </h4>
                <p className="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                  Classical electromagnetism says an accelerating charge
                  radiates energy. An electron orbiting a nucleus would lose
                  energy and spiral inward in a fraction of a second — atoms
                  should not be stable. The model also could not explain the
                  sharp, discrete lines in atomic spectra.
                </p>
              </div>

              {/* Bohr Model */}
              <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-10 mb-4">
                <Orbit className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-500" />
                Bohr's quantized orbits (1913)
              </h4>

              <p>
                Niels Bohr rescued the atom by declaring that electrons can
                occupy only certain allowed orbits, where they do not radiate.
              </p>

              <div className="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 my-6">
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/40 p-4">
                  <span className="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                    Postulate 1
                  </span>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                    Electrons move in stationary circular orbits without losing
                    energy.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/40 p-4">
                  <span className="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                    Postulate 2
                  </span>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                    Angular momentum is quantized:{" "}
                    <strong>mvr = nh/2π</strong>, so only certain orbits are
                    allowed.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/40 p-4">
                  <span className="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                    Postulate 3
                  </span>
                  <p className="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                    A jump between levels absorbs or emits a photon with energy{" "}
                    <strong>ΔE = hν</strong>.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div className="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-6 my-6">
                <h4 className="m-0 mb-5 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                  Hydrogen energy levels
                </h4>
                <div className="space-y-3">
                  {hydrogenLevels.map((level) => (
                    <div key={level.level} className="flex items-center gap-3">
                      <span className="w-16 shrink-0 text-right font-mono text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                        {level.level}
                      </span>
                      <div className="flex-1">
                        <div
                          className={`h-2.5 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-green-500 to-teal-500 ${level.width}`}
                        />
                      </div>
                      <span className="w-20 shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                        {level.energy}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
                <div className="mt-5 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-xl bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-900/20 p-3">
                  <RefreshCw className="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-green-600 dark:text-green-400" />
                  <p className="m-0 text-xs leading-relaxed text-green-800 dark:text-green-300">
                    An electron dropping from n = 3 to n = 2 releases a photon
                    of ΔE = 1.89 eV — the red 656 nm line of hydrogen.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p className="text-sm">
                <strong>Success:</strong> Bohr's model explained the hydrogen
                spectrum and introduced quantized energy levels.{" "}
                <strong>Limitations:</strong> it only works for one-electron
                systems (H, He⁺, Li²⁺); it cannot explain multi-electron atoms,
                fine structure, or the Zeeman effect.
              </p>

              {/* Quantum Mechanical Model */}
              <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-10 mb-4">
                <Waves className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-500" />
                The quantum mechanical model (1926)
              </h4>

              <div className="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] md:items-center my-6">
                <div className="relative mx-auto h-40 w-40">
                  <div className="absolute inset-0 rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(16,185,129,0.55)_0%,rgba(20,184,166,0.25)_45%,transparent_72%)] blur-sm" />
                  <div className="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
                    1s orbital
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <p className="mt-0">
                    Schrödinger's wave equation describes the electron as a
                    standing wave. The square of the wavefunction gives the
                    probability of finding the electron at a point.
                  </p>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-2 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li className="flex gap-2">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-green-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong>1924:</strong> de Broglie proposes matter waves.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li className="flex gap-2">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong>1926:</strong> Schrödinger writes the wave
                        equation; orbitals replace orbits.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li className="flex gap-2">
                      <span className="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-emerald-500" />
                      <span>
                        <strong>1927:</strong> Heisenberg's uncertainty
                        principle rules out definite electron paths.
                      </span>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              {/* Key Takeaway */}
              <div className="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 my-8 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-5 text-xl">
                  <Target className="text-blue-500" />
                  Key Takeaway: What Survived the Model Wars
                </h4>
                <div className="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
                  <div className="rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-4 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                    <p className="m-0 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                      A nuclear atom
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0 mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      A tiny, dense, positive nucleus surrounded by electrons.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <div className="rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-4 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                    <p className="m-0 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                      Quantized energy
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0 mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      Electrons occupy discrete energy levels, not a continuum.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <div className="rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-4 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                    <p className="m-0 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                      Probability orbitals
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0 mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                      We describe where an electron is likely to be, not a
                      precise orbit.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              {/* Real World Example */}
              <div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 to-orange-50 dark:from-amber-900/20 dark:to-orange-900/20 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 my-8 border border-amber-200/50 dark:border-amber-700/30">
                <div className="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div className="p-3 bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-800/50 rounded-xl text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mt-1">
                    <Lightbulb size={24} />
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 className="text-lg font-bold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300 mb-2 m-0">
                      Real-World Example: Why Neon Signs Glow
                    </h4>
                    <p className="m-0 text-amber-800/80 dark:text-amber-200/80 leading-relaxed">
                      Electric current excites neon electrons into higher energy
                      levels. When they fall back, they emit photons at specific
                      wavelengths. Bohr's quantized jumps are exactly why each
                      gas glows with its own signature colour: neon red-orange,
                      argon blue, krypton pale violet.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <Exercise
                number="2.2"
                accent="blue"
                question={
                  <p className="m-0">
                    In Rutherford's gold-foil experiment, why did most alpha
                    particles pass through undeflected while a very small
                    fraction bounced back?
                  </p>
                }
                answer={
                  <div className="space-y-2">
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>Most passed through</strong> because the atom is
                      mostly empty space; an alpha particle rarely comes close
                      to a nucleus.
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0">
                      <strong>A few bounced back</strong> because they
                      approached a tiny, dense region of concentrated positive
                      charge — the nucleus. The strong electrostatic repulsion
                      reversed their direction of motion.
                    </p>
                    <p className="m-0">
                      The large-angle deflections also showed that this
                      positive charge contains most of the atom's mass.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                }
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Section 2.3 */}
        <motion.section
          variants={itemVariants}
          id="subtopic-2.3"
          className="scroll-mt-24"
        >
          <div className={cardClass}>
            <div className={sectionHeaderClass}>
              <div
                className={`${numberBoxClass} bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400`}
              >
                2.3
              </div>
              <h3 className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                Quantum Numbers
              </h3>
            </div>

            <div className={proseClass}>
              <p className="lead text-xl text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium mb-8">
                Four quantum numbers work like a postal address for an
                electron. Together they specify its shell, subshell, orbital,
                and spin.
              </p>

              <p>
                The quantum mechanical model replaces Bohr's circular orbits
                with three-dimensional probability regions called{" "}
                <strong>orbitals</strong>. Solving the Schrödinger equation
                produces four quantum numbers that completely describe an
                electron's state in an atom.
              </p>

              {/* Four Quantum Number Cards */}
              <div className="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 my-8">
                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-purple-100 dark:border-purple-800/60 bg-purple-50/40 dark:bg-purple-900/10 p-5">
                  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                    <div className="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/50 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">
                      <Sigma className="h-4 w-4" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 className="m-0 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                        Principal quantum number (n)
                      </h4>
                      <p className="m-0 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">
                        The shell
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-1.5 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li>
                      Allowed values: <strong>1, 2, 3, …</strong>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Determines the shell (K, L, M, N…) and the main energy and
                      size of the orbital.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Maximum electrons in the shell: <strong>2n²</strong>.
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 dark:border-blue-800/60 bg-blue-50/40 dark:bg-blue-900/10 p-5">
                  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                    <div className="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/50 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                      <Layers className="h-4 w-4" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 className="m-0 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                        Angular momentum number (l)
                      </h4>
                      <p className="m-0 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                        The subshell
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-1.5 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li>
                      Allowed values: <strong>0 to n − 1</strong>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Determines the subshell type: l = 0 (s), 1 (p), 2 (d), 3
                      (f).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      A shell with principal number n contains{" "}
                      <strong>n subshells</strong> and sets the orbital shape.
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-rose-100 dark:border-rose-800/60 bg-rose-50/40 dark:bg-rose-900/10 p-5">
                  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                    <div className="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-rose-100 dark:bg-rose-900/50 text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400">
                      <Magnet className="h-4 w-4" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 className="m-0 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                        Magnetic quantum number (m<sub>l</sub>)
                      </h4>
                      <p className="m-0 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400">
                        The orbital
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-1.5 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li>
                      Allowed values: <strong>−l to +l</strong>, including 0.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Determines the orientation of the orbital in space.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Number of orbitals in a subshell:{" "}
                      <strong>2l + 1</strong>.
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div className="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100 dark:border-amber-800/60 bg-amber-50/40 dark:bg-amber-900/10 p-5">
                  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                    <div className="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/50 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">
                      <RefreshCw className="h-4 w-4" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 className="m-0 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                        Spin quantum number (m<sub>s</sub>)
                      </h4>
                      <p className="m-0 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">
                        The spin
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <ul className="m-0 space-y-1.5 pl-0 list-none text-sm">
                    <li>
                      Allowed values: <strong>+½ or −½</strong>.
                    </li>
                    <li>Describes the electron's spin orientation.</li>
                    <li>
                      An orbital holds at most <strong>2 electrons</strong>{" "}
                      with opposite spins.
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              {/* Worked Example */}
              <div className="rounded-2xl border border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-800/60 bg-purple-50/50 dark:bg-purple-900/15 p-5 sm:p-6 my-8">
                <h4 className="m-0 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-bold text-purple-900 dark:text-purple-300">
                  <Sigma className="h-4 w-4" />
                  Worked Example: Unpack the n = 3 shell
                </h4>
                <div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">
                  {[
                    { label: "Allowed l", value: "0, 1, 2" },
                    { label: "Subshells", value: "3s, 3p, 3d" },
                    { label: "Orbitals", value: "1 + 3 + 5 = 9" },
                    { label: "Max electrons", value: "9 × 2 = 18" },
                  ].map((step) => (
                    <div
                      key={step.label}
                      className="rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-3 border border-purple-100 dark:border-purple-800/60"
                    >
                      <p className="m-0 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-purple-500 dark:text-purple-400">
                        {step.label}
                      </p>
                      <p className="m-0 mt-1 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                        {step.value}
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
                <p className="m-0 mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                  For the 3d subshell (l = 2), m<sub>l</sub> can be −2, −1, 0,
                  +1, +2 — five orbitals, each holding two electrons.
                </p>
              </div>

              {/* Subshell Table */}
              <h4 className="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">
                <Table2 className="h-5 w-5 text-purple-500" />
                Subshell quick reference
              </h4>

              <div className="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
                <table className="w-full min-w-[520px] text-sm m-0">
                  <thead className="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800">
                    <tr>
                      <th className="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
                        Subshell
                      </th>
                      <th className="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
                        l value
                      </th>
                      <th className="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
